[{"name":"MultiGrid","type":"structure","meta":{"uuid":"2d17faff-1ae4-498f-8e85-c5b9631d76bd","isGlobalTemplate":false},"configuration":{"columnWidths":[3,9],"layout":{"gap":"L","marginTop":0,"marginBottom":0,"backgroundColor":"transparent"},"visible":true},"content":[{"name":"DetailsList","type":"structure","meta":{"uuid":"c840d772-9ecd-48b4-8685-cd51889f1224","isGlobalTemplate":false},"configuration":{"visible":true,"layout":{"fullWidth":false,"caretPosition":"right"}},"content":[{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"6f172896-0564-4ce6-acda-1bfa4978743d","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>Both are 2 mm round laces made of cotton; the difference lies in the waxing. The R2-SL runs more slowly through the wax bath and soaks up more wax. It is double-waxed and has a special depth of colour and a splendid sheen like fine calfskin.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">In the hand, the R2-SL is grippier and firmer at first. That is part of a heavily waxed lace; it becomes supple with wear. The R2-CS gets our standard waxing: waxed, hot-rolled and polished, with a silky-matt sheen. The R2-SL is made in Italy.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> CS &amp; SL&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 560px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Feature</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">R2-CS Classic Sportive</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">R2-SL Splendore di Laccico</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Waxing<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Finish</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Waxed, hot-rolled and polished.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Double-waxed: longer wax bath, more polishing.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Sheen<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Look</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Silky matt.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Splendid sheen like fine calfskin, special depth of colour.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Grip<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Feel</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Grippy, becomes softer with wear.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Noticeably grippier and firmer at first, becomes supple with wear.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Suits<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Shoes</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Oxfords, Derbies, dress shoes for every day.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Goodyear-welted Oxfords and Derbies in box calf or shell cordovan.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Lengths<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Range</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">45–180 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">45–180 cm</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"What distinguishes the Splendore di Laccico series (R2-SL) technically and in feel from the R2-CS series?","defaultOpen":false}}},{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"9f8bb320-f3d4-4c1c-9f6e-24d38c1cbde7","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>2 mm round laces go well with classic lace-up shoes with concealed eyelets: Oxfords, Derbies, full brogues and fine lace-up ankle boots, for women and men alike.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">With concealed eyelets (blind eyelets) you only see a small hole in the leather from above, with a fine eyelet underneath. The 2 mm round lace is made for these. The long lengths up to 180 cm mostly go to women's boots. Sneakers and boots have visible eyelets or hooks; there, thicker laces are the better choice.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Shoe types&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 560px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Shoe</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Eyelets</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Series</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Good to know</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Oxfords<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Closed lacing</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Concealed eyelets</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">The classic among dress shoes.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Derbies<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Open lacing</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Mostly concealed eyelets</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">In the classic segment almost always with a 2 mm round lace.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Full brogues<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Perforations, decorative stitching</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Today mostly concealed eyelets</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Often a full brogue is meant: check the eyelets first.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Lace-up ankle boots<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Fine, for women and men</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Concealed eyelets</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Usually 120 cm, women's boots up to 180 cm.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Sneakers, boots<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">For comparison</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Visible eyelets, hooks</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-3-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R3-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/flat-laces-by-width/flat-laces-4-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">F4-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/flat-laces-by-width/flat-laces-6-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">F6</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Thicker laces fit here.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"Which shoes go best with 2 mm round laces?","defaultOpen":false}}},{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"07bebaf2-ed39-4b40-b1b3-090a3d798aab","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>You use a 2 mm round lace when the shoe has concealed eyelets. The lace should pass easily through the eyelet, otherwise its surface is put under heavy strain when it is pulled through.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">You can recognise concealed eyelets by the fact that no metal ring is visible on the outside, only a small hole in the leather. For the length, the safest way is to measure the old laces unlaced, from tip to tip. For classic footwear, the number of pairs of eyelets serves as a rule of thumb; for women's sizes, rather one size shorter.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Lengths for R2&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 560px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Pairs of eyelets</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Length</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Typical shoes</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Series</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">1–2<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">pairs of eyelets</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">45 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Shoes with only one pair of holes</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">3–4<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">pairs of eyelets</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">60 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Derbies with low-set lacing panels</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">4–5<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">pairs of eyelets</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">75 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Classic Derbies and Oxfords with 5 pairs of holes</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">5–6<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">pairs of eyelets</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">90 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Derbies and Oxfords for a wider foot, transition to ankle-high shoes</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">7–8<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">pairs of eyelets</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">120 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Lace-up ankle boots</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">from 9<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">pairs of eyelets / boots</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">150–180 cm</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Tall lace-up boots, mostly women's boots</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"When do you use a 2 mm round lace (R2)?","defaultOpen":false}}},{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"207adc89-7ece-484a-bddc-1e1894e84007","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>Splendore di Laccico suits fine, classic shoes in smooth leather: Goodyear-welted Oxfords, Derbies and full brogues in box calf or shell cordovan, as well as evening shoes and fine women's ankle boots.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">It is double-waxed and made in Italy. Its sheen and depth of colour recall well-cared-for calfskin, and the colours carry their Italian names, from Bianco to Grigio Ferro. The lace a good shoe expects. Like all 2 mm round laces, it is made for concealed eyelets, in lengths from 45 to 180 cm.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Shoes for SL&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 560px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Leather &amp; shoe</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Series</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Box calf<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Polished calfskin</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Sheen and depth of colour suit the polished leather.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Shell cordovan<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">For connoisseurs</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">The deep sheen of cordovan finds its counterpart here.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Evening shoes<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Dinner jacket, tailcoat, special occasions</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">A fine lace for formal wear.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">Women's ankle boots<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Fine, with concealed eyelets</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Long lengths up to 180 cm, also for boots.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"Which shoes suit the exclusive Splendore di Laccico (SL) style?","defaultOpen":false}}},{"name":"TextCard","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"918371b5-2427-47a6-bc0f-fab7bacfaab7","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"text":{"htmlDescription":"<div class=\"mb-2\"><p class=\"mb-2\"><strong>The 2 mm round lace is barely noticeable and lets the leather and shape of the shoe speak. The 3 mm round lace is visibly stronger and suits shoes that are themselves more sturdily built.</strong></p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><p class=\"mb-2\">The effect follows the eyelet: concealed eyelets on fine low shoes call for the 2 mm round lace, visible eyelets and hooks on lace-up ankle boots and boots for the 3 mm round lace. And the longer the lace, the more of it you see. On a low shoe it remains a detail; on an ankle boot it becomes a surface.</p><p class=\"mb-2\"><br></p><div class=\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center d-md-none bg-light p-2 mb-2 border rounded\"><span class=\"small font-weight-bold text-dark\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right text-muted mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> 2 mm &amp; 3 mm&nbsp;</span> <span class=\"badge badge-secondary py-1 px-2\">&nbsp;<i class=\"fa fa-arrows-h mr-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Swipe sideways&nbsp;</span></div></div><div class=\"laccico-scroll-wrapper\"><div class=\"table-responsive laccico-scroll-table\"><table class=\"table table-bordered table-hover text-left mb-0\" style=\"border: 1px solid #000000; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 680px;\"><thead class=\"thead-dark\" style=\"background-color: #000000; color: #ffffff;\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Lace</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Series</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Effect</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Eyelets</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"py-3 px-3\">Lengths</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">2 mm round<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Classic Sportive, Splendore</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-cs\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-CS</a> · <a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-2-mm/r2-sl\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R2-SL</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Fine, barely noticeable.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Concealed eyelets</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">45–180 cm</td></tr><tr><td class=\"font-weight-bold py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\">3 mm round<br><span class=\"small text-muted font-weight-normal\">Classic Sportive</span></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle text-nowrap\"><a href=\"/en/shape-diameter/round-laces-by-diameter/round-laces-3-mm\" class=\"font-weight-bold text-dark d-block\" style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">R3-CS</a></td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Strong, clearly visible.</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">Visible eyelets and hooks</td><td class=\"py-3 px-3 align-middle\">45–150 cm</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","textAlignment":"left","color":""},"button":{"label":"","link":"","variant":"primary"},"layout":{"backgroundColor":"","paddingTop":0,"paddingBottom":0,"paddingLeft":0,"paddingRight":0}},"configuration":{"visible":true,"detailsSettings":{"label":"How does the look of 2 mm round laces differ from that of 3 mm round laces?","defaultOpen":false}}}],"parent_slot":0},{"name":"CategoryData","type":"content","meta":{"uuid":"aa279f63-76a0-43b5-9b38-e2a80f6eacd3","isGlobalTemplate":false},"content":{"name":"","fields":{"name":true,"description1":true,"description2":false,"shortDescription":false},"fieldsOrder":["name","description1","description2","shortDescription"],"fieldsDisabled":[],"displayCategoryImage":"off","image":{"fillMode":"fill","alt":"","brightness":0.75},"text":{"color":"#121212","bgColor":"#fbfbf9","bgOpacity":1,"textAlignm